Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:34:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV cache: a restored layout is
 checked once and only its unwritten slots are zeroed

install_restored_history ran the layout check for every layer's cache and
zeroed every live slot before the restore overwrote the attended ones (the
whole history's K/V: 6.9 GB of writes at 8 CausVid chunks, on the forward's
stream ahead of the restore). The check is now cached per layout value (a
restore installs one layout into 30 caches; a cached plan reuses it across
requests), and only the live slots no span writes (live, not attended:
evicted by the next append before any read) are zeroed. The attended slots
must be written in full by write() or by the backend before the first read,
as both the plain and the layer-overlapped restore do. Step 11 F5 cut 5
(coordinator 17:40).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
